From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:43:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cpu/intel/haswell: Lock the soft reset straps at every boot
 and resume

SOFT_RESET_DATA and SOFT_RESET_CTRL stay writable after the boot: on a
ThinkPad W541 under Linux, SOFT_RESET_LOCK (RCBA + 0x38F0) reads 0 and
the straps written from the OS (the second threads, the active cores,
the flex ratio) apply at the next warm reset, and at the next resume
from S3. The Lenovo firmware of the W541 (GNET94WW, CpuInitPeim and
PchInitDxe) sets SOFT_RESET_LOCK bit 0 at every boot, and again on S3
resume through its boot script; model_206ax locks it too.

Lock it in romstage once the Hyper-Threading option is applied, and on
S3 resume, where romstage does not look at the option. A reset clears
the lock, so the next boot can still change the straps.

TEST=Build of the ThinkPad W541 with the native RAM init.

Change-Id: I4919b8b56002b2724d6835eb97c6d1f57a61a70f
---
 src/cpu/intel/haswell/haswell.h          |  2 ++
 src/cpu/intel/haswell/hyperthreading.c   | 12 ++++++++++++
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/romstage.c |  1 +
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.h    |  1 +
 4 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cpu/intel/haswell/haswell.h b/src/cpu/intel/haswell/haswell.h
index e3d362f51c..d0554f63d3 100644
--- a/src/cpu/intel/haswell/haswell.h
+++ b/src/cpu/intel/haswell/haswell.h
@@ -245,6 +245,8 @@ void haswell_check_vmx_option(void);
 void haswell_check_ht_option(void);
 /* Whether the last boot ended with that reset, before any memory init */
 bool haswell_ht_reset_was_last(void);
+/* Lock the soft reset straps until the next reset, at every boot and resume */
+void haswell_lock_soft_reset(void);
 /* A second thread per core, on or turned off by the option, for the menu */
 bool haswell_ht_available(void);
 
diff --git a/src/cpu/intel/haswell/hyperthreading.c b/src/cpu/intel/haswell/hyperthreading.c
index 730be3628a..b8a3913f21 100644
--- a/src/cpu/intel/haswell/hyperthreading.c
+++ b/src/cpu/intel/haswell/hyperthreading.c
@@ -44,6 +44,18 @@ bool haswell_ht_reset_was_last(void)
 	return code == POSTCODE_RESET_REQUESTED && extra == RESET_EXTRA_HYPER_THREADING;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Lock SOFT_RESET_DATA and SOFT_RESET_CTRL until the next reset, as the Lenovo
+ * firmware of the ThinkPad W541 does at every boot and resume: unlocked, the OS
+ * can write the straps (the second threads, the active cores, the flex ratio)
+ * for the next warm reset, or for the next resume from S3, where they apply
+ * too. A reset clears the lock, so the next boot can still change them.
+ */
+void haswell_lock_soft_reset(void)
+{
+	RCBA32_OR(SOFT_RESET_LOCK, 1);
+}
+
 bool haswell_ht_available(void)
 {
 	/* haswell_check_ht_option() needs CMOS_POST: without it, no option */
diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/romstage.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/romstage.c
index bb63ab86e4..0c4814d6c6 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/romstage.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/romstage.c
@@ -158,6 +158,7 @@ void mainboard_romstage_entry(void)
 		haswell_check_vmx_option();
 		haswell_check_ht_option();
 	}
+	haswell_lock_soft_reset();
 
 	/* After the resets of the options, before the memory init */
 	firmware_watchdog_romstage(s3resume);
diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.h b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.h
index 4dccc575f5..920bc3d947 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.h
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.h
@@ -504,6 +504,7 @@ void mainboard_config_rcba(void);
 #define  PM_CFG2_DRAM_RESET_CTL	(1 << 26)	/* ULT only */
 #define PMSYNC_CONFIG	0x33c4	/* 32bit */
 #define PMSYNC_CONFIG2	0x33cc	/* 32bit */
+#define SOFT_RESET_LOCK 0x38f0
 #define SOFT_RESET_CTRL 0x38f4
 #define SOFT_RESET_DATA 0x38f8
 
-- 
2.43.0

